@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Who uses Azure DevOps?";
    Layout = "~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureLayout.cshtml";
}

@await Html.PartialAsync("~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureContentStyles.cshtml")

<div class="row g-4">
    <aside class="col-lg-3">
        @Html.Partial("~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureTopics.cshtml")
    </aside>
    <section class="col-lg-9">
        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm">
            <div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">
                <div class="azure-notes-content">
                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">Who uses Azure DevOps?
Azure DevOps can be used by any team who wants to make the workflow automate most
primarily Azure DevOps is used by the Software Develops, DevOps Engineers, and Testing
Engineers.
When coming to organizations there are some famous organizations that are using Azure
DevOps some of them are mentioned below.
   •   Netflix: Netflix is a company that will have continuous updates on the source code to
       satisfy their customers by using Azure DevOps will reduce the cost and time of the
       company and can deliver most efficiently to the end users.
   •   Microsoft: We all know that Microsoft is one of the biggest organizations in the
       whole world it is very important for them to reduce the latency or give a hundred
       percent to the users who are using Microsoft products it can be achieved easily with
       the help of Azure DevOps.
The above are a few companies that are currently using Azure DevOps. other than that there
are more companies like Google, Uber, and so on which are using Azure DevOps.</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    

            @await Html.PartialAsync("~/Areas/Azure/Views/Shared/AzureLessonNavigation.cshtml")
</section>
</div>
<style>
.azure-notes-text{white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:normal;font-family:inherit;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.7;background:#fff;border:0;padding:0;margin:0;color:#212529;}
.azure-notes-content img{max-height:720px;}
</style>